-- title:
--   Local quasi-finiteness of [n] on fibres of relative Pic⁰
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a nonzero natural number $M$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and a witness $hj$ that the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ` (the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}$ times the integral power series `jNum`) lies in `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`, the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the integral form ratios for $SL_2(\mathbb{Z})$; this makes `jAt` available and hence the two-chart integral model $X$ of level $\Gamma_M(M,H)$ with its structure morphism $c =$ `toBase p (ΓM M H) hj` to $\operatorname{Spec} R_p$. Let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a bundle `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj` of properties of this model, with its rigidified section $\mathfrak{X}.\varepsilon_{\inf}$ over the identity of the base. Let $D$ consist of a scheme $P$, a morphism $D.\mathrm{toBase} : P \to \operatorname{Spec} R_p$ and a section of it, and let $hD$ assert that $D$ represents the relative Picard functor cut out by `algEquivZeroCut`: a Poincaré rigidified line bundle on the pullback of $c$ along $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ whose fibres are algebraically equivalent to zero, such that every $\varepsilon_{\inf}$-rigidified line bundle over a base $t$ with that fibrewise property is induced, up to isomorphism of underlying line bundles, by a unique morphism over $\operatorname{Spec} R_p$ into $D.\mathrm{toBase}$, and the zero section pulls the Poincaré bundle back to the unit. Assume $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ smooth. Let $s$ be a point of $\operatorname{Spec} R_p$ and $n \ge 1$ a natural number whose image in the residue field at $s$ is not a unit. Then the endomorphism $[n]$ — `schemeNsmul n`, the $n$-fold sum of the identity point — of the fibre at $s$ of the relative group law on $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ determined by $hD$ (group law obtained from the group-object structure for `algEquivZeroGroupCut`), a relative group law over the residue field of $s$, is locally quasi-finite.
--
--   This is the fibrewise input for multiplication by $n$ on the relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_H(M)$ at a prime $p$ exactly dividing $M$, where the special fibre is not an abelian variety and $[n]$ need only be quasi-finite rather than finite. It is consumed by [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.nsmul_flat_surjective_locallyQuasiFinite_of_representsRelSubPic`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.nsmul_flat_surjective_locallyQuasiFinite_of_representsRelSubPic), which upgrades local quasi-finiteness on all fibres to flatness, surjectivity and local quasi-finiteness of $[n]$ over the base.
